$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Paal-Knorr pyrrole
cyclocondensation. In a typical reaction, primary aromatic amine (1
mmol), hexane-2,5-dione (1.2 mmol) and L-tryptophan (0.04 g, 0.2 mmol)
were stirred at 70 °C for the appropriate reaction time. After completion
of the reaction (monitored by TLC or GC), ethanol (2 mL) was added to the
reaction mixture and the catalyst was recovered by filtration. The
organic medium was removed with a rotary evaporator under reduced
pressure. N-(4'-bromomethylphenyl)-2,5-dimethylpyrrole (1j). 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.65 (d, 2H, J = 8.5 Hz), 7.10 (d, 2H, J = 8.5 Hz), 5.92
(s, 2H), 2.04 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 138.0, 132.2, 129.8,
128.6, 121.5, 106.0, 12.9; MS (EI), m/z (rel. intensity %) 251 (M+, 80),
250 (100), 249 (78), 169 (30), 154 (30), 129 (20). M. p.: 75°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, Paal-Knorr pyrrole cyclocondensation, no solvent,
recyclable catalyst, optimization study, optimized on temperature,
optimized on time, optimized on stoichiometry of catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM L-Tryptophan-catalyzed Paal-Knorr pyrrole cyclocondensation: an
efficient, clean and recyclable organocatalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
