$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the acid-catalyzed
Paal-Knorr pyrrole cyclocondensation Vitamin B1 (0.05 mmol) was well
stirred in ethanol (2 mL) for a few minutes. Primary amine (1 mmol) and
hexane-2,5-dione (1.2 mmol) were then added, and the mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 1 h. The progress of the reaction was monitored
by thin-layer chromatography or gas chromatography. The organic medium
was removed with a rotary evaporator under reduced pressure. Water (5 mL)
was added to the resulting solid mixture and extracted with ethyl acetate
to afford the product 1. The crude product was passed through a short
column of neutral alumina [eluted with ethyl acetate/hexane (3:7)] to
give the pure products. N-(4'-methylphenyl)-2,5-dimethylpyrrole (1c)
[CASRegistry No. 5044-26-8], yield 95%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.40
(d, J = 15.8 Hz, 2H), 7.24 (d, J = 15.8 Hz, 2H), 6.06 (s, 2H), 2.59 (s,
3H), 2.19 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (125 MHz,CDCl3) δ 137.3, 136.2, 129.5, 127.7,
105.4, 21.0, 12.9; MS (EI), m/z (rel. intensity %) 185 (M+, 75), 184
(100), 170 (15), 154 (10), 129 (20), 91 (10), 77 (5).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, conversion, 100%, Paal-Knorr pyrrole synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Vitamin B1 as a metal-free organocatalyst for greener Paal-Knorr pyrrole
synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Darabi, Hossein Reza; Aghapoor, Kioumars; Darestani Farahani, Abbas;
Mohsenzadeh, Farshid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Environmental Chemistry Letters (2012), 10(4), 369-375

