$DATUM 75-05-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis and characterization of polysubstitued furans To a dry Schlenk
tube that charged with nitrogen, 1,4-dione 4 (0.2 mmol) was added, then
freshly distilled CH3CN (2.0 mL) was injected through a syringe.
Subsequently, TfOH (17.3 μL, 0.2 mmol) was added to the mixture, and the
resulting solution was stirred at 85 °C for 1 h. Then the resulting
solution was cooled to room temperature, and solvent was evaporated under
vacuum, the residue was purified by flash column chromatography on silica
gel (eluent: ethyl acetate/ petroleum ether). The furan 5
(2,5-Diphenylfuran-3-yl)(phenyl)methanone (5a): 13 Isolated by flash
column chromatography (ethyl acetate/petroleum ether = 1:10) in 93%
yield. Yellow oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.89 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H),
7.79-7.74 (m, 4H), 7.52 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 7.44-7.38 (m, 4H), 7.35-7.28
(m, 4H), 6.93 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 191.8, 154.9, 152.4,
137.9, 132.9, 129.7, 129.0, 128.8, 128.4, 128.3, 128.1, 127.4, 124.0,
122.8, 108.6. Rf = 0.5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Paal-Knorr furan synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Rearrangement of tert-Butylperoxides for the Construction of
Polysubstituted Furans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zheng, Xiaojian; Lu, Shenglin; Li, Zhiping
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(21), 5432-5435

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME94 STEP1
$RXN



