$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis and characterization of
polysubstitued furans To a dry Schlenk tube that charged with nitrogen,
1,4-dione 4 (0.2 mmol) was added, then freshly distilled CH3CN (2.0 mL)
was injected through a syringe. Subsequently, TfOH (17.3 μL, 0.2 mmol)
was added to the mixture, and the resulting solution was stirred at 85 °C
for 1 h. Then the resulting solution was cooled to room temperature, and
solvent was evaporated under vacuum, the residue was purified by flash
column chromatography on silica gel (eluent: ethyl acetate/ petroleum
ether). The furan 5 2,5-Diphenylfuran (5d): [15] Isolated by flash column
chromatography (ethyl acetate/petroleum ether = 1:10) in 90% yield.
Yellow oil. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.77 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 4H), 7.42 (t,
J = 7.6 Hz, 4H), 7.29 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 6.76 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
100 MHz): δ 153.3, 130.7, 128.7, 127.3, 123.7, 107.2. Rf = 0.5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Paal-Knorr furan synthesis
