$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Scheme 1. General Synthetic Approach to
Pyrrolonesa A. General procedure for the microwave-accelerated synthesis
of 2,5-dimethyl-1-aryl-1H-pyrroles(6). 2,5-Hexandione (4) (1 mmol), the
appropriate aniline 5a-x (1.2 equiv) and p-toluenesulfonic acid bound
with silica gel (0.4 equiv) were mixed in an oven dried pressure vial
with a magnetic stirrer bar. The vessel was placed in a microwave oven
and heated (180 °C, 15-20 min) under microwave irradiation (0-400 W at
2.45 GHz). After stirring for a further 15 min at room temperature the
reaction mixture was filtered and the residual silica washed with DCM (10
mL). The solvent was removed under reduced pressure to give the
corresponding 2,5-dimethyl-1-aryl-1H-pyrrole 6a-x (80-90% yield, purity
&gt;95% by LCMS). B. General Procedure for the synthesis of formyl
pyrroles (7a-r). Phosphorous oxychloride (0.5 mL, 6 mmol) was added
dropwise to stirred ice-cooled DMF (12 mL) under a N2 atmosphere. The
mixture was then allowed to warm to room temperature over 15 min, a
solution of the pyrrole (6a-r) (1 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) added and the
mixture heated at 100 °C for 3 h under a N2 atmosphere. After cooling,
30% aq NaOH was added dropwise to pH 10.0 and the resulting precipitate
was filtered, washed several times with water and dried in vacuo to give
the corresponding formyl derivative 7a-r (80-95%), which was generally
used without further purification. Scheme 1. General Synthetic Approach
to Pyrrolonesa Scheme 1. General Synthetic Approach to Pyrrolonesa
Compound 7t, yield 95%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (0W-400W) (stage 1), solid-supported catalyst
(stage 1), no solvent (stage 1), pressure vial used (stage 1), Paal-Knorr
pyrrole synthesis (stage 1), silica gel support used (stage 1),
Vilsmeier-Haack formylation (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery and Structure-Activity Relationships of Pyrrolone Antimalarials
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Murugesan, Dinakaran; Mital, Alka; Kaiser, Marcel; Shackleford, David M.;
Morizzi, Julia; Katneni, Kasiram; Campbell, Michael; Hudson, Alan;
Charman, Susan A.; Yeates, Clive; Gilbert, Ian H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Medicinal Chemistry (2013), 56(7), 2975-2990

