$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-Ethyl
5-[[2,5-dimethyl-1-(4-methylsulfinylphenyl)pyrrol-3-yl]methylene]-2-methyl-4-oxo-
2,5-Hexandione (4) (1 mmol), the appropriate aniline 5a-x (1.2 equiv) and
p-toluenesulfonic acid bound with silica gel (0.4 equiv) were mixed in an
oven dried pressure vial with a magnetic stirrer bar. The vessel was
placed in a microwave oven and heated (180 °C, 15-20 min) under microwave
irradiation (0-400 W at 2.45 GHz). After stirring for a further 15 min at
room temperature the reaction mixture was filtered and the residual
silica washed with DCM (10 mL). The solvent was removed under reduced
pressure to give the corresponding 2,5-dimethyl-1-aryl-1H-pyrrole 6a-x
(80-90% yield, purity &gt;95% by LCMS). Phosphorous oxychloride (0.5 mL,
6 mmol) was added dropwise to stirred ice-cooled DMF (12 mL) under a N2
atmosphere. The mixture was then allowed to warm to room temperature over
15 min, a solution of the pyrrole (6a-r) (1 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) added and
the mixture heated at 100 °C for 3 h under a N2 atmosphere. After
cooling, 30% aq NaOH was added dropwise to pH 10.0 and the resulting
precipitate was filtered, washed several times with water and dried in
vacuo to give the corresponding formyl derivative 7a-r (80-95%), which
was generally used without further purification. To a solution of ethyl
5-methyl-3-oxo-1,2-dihydropyrrole-4-carboxylate (3) (1.0 equiv) in
absolute ethanol (3 mL) was added 2,5-dimethyl-1-aryl/substituted
aryl-3-formylpyrroles (7a-r) (1.0 equiv) and potassium hydrogen sulphate
(0.2 equiv). The reaction mixture was heated at 70-80 °C for 3 h,
resulting in the formation of a yellow precipitate. The mixture was
poured on to crushed ice, the solid filtered and dried in vacuo to afford
the corresponding ethyl (5E)-5-[[2,5-dimethyl-1-[Substituted
phenyl]pyrrol-3-yl]methylene]-2-methyl-4-oxo-1H-pyrrole-3-carboxylate
(8a-r) (80-95% yield), generally as yellow powders, with purity &gt;95%,
as determined by LC-MS. (E)-Ethyl
5-[[2,5-dimethyl-1-(4-methylsulfinylphenyl)pyrrol-3-yl]methylene]-2-methyl-4-oxo-1H-pyrrole-3-carboxylate
(8o). Yield 95%. mp 150-155 °C. 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 10.28 (s,
1H, -NH), 7.88-7.87 (d, 2H), 7.59-7.58 (d, 2H), 6.74 (s, 1H), 6.70 (s,
1H), 4.13-4.09 (m, 2H, J = 7.05 Hz), 2.85 (brs, 3H), 2.59 (s, 3H), 2.13
(brs, 3H), 2.09 (s, 3H), 1.23-1.21 (t, 3H, J = 1.25, 5.80 Hz). 13C NMR
(125 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 180.45, 170.12, 163.30, 146.45, 138.93, 134.70,
130.60, 129.15, 128.78, 124.94, 113.77, 109.62, 106.44, 102.44, 58.18,
15.82, 14.43, 12.63, 10.77. HRMS (m/z): [MH+] calcd for C22H25N2O4S,
413.1530; found 413.1517.
